## Eight men on a raft (eight-men-raft), generated from the Rosie teaching script (english-input.txt) under the world conventions.
##
## Instructor statements used (numbers as in english-input.txt):
##   4. If a clear location is to the right of a blue peg then you can move the peg onto the location.
##   5. If a location is not below an object then it is clear.
##   6. If an object is a block then it is a peg.
##   7. If a clear location is to the left of a red peg then you can move the peg onto the location.
##   9. If a red peg is to the right of a peg and the peg is to the right of a clear location then you can move the red peg onto the clear location.
##  10. If a blue peg is to the left of a peg and the peg is to the left of a clear location then you can move the blue peg onto the clear location.
##  15. The goal is that all the red blocks are on the red locations and all the blue blocks are on the blue locations.
## World: init-8men.world (nine locations in a row; four blue pegs, a clear location, four red pegs)
##
## Translation (tools/rosie-language.md gives the general reading; the assumption ledger is in README.md):
##   - Operator move (argument1 = the peg, argument2 = the clear location it moves onto); four proposals, one per move
##     statement (4, 7, 9, 10). Every block is a peg (statement 6). Blue pegs step right and jump right over any peg; red pegs
##     step left and jump left over any peg.
##   - clear is a maintained one-argument relation (statement 5); left-of and right-of are static relations between locations,
##     and a peg is to the left/right of a location when the location it is on is (A-S1).
##   - The goal (statement 15) is expanded over the blocks of the world file (A-S2). "The solution has twenty-four steps"
##     (statement 11) is checked against the plans, not used.
## Matching hints for learned rules (World-Conventions L3-095, L11-009): many-valued attributes, sized from the initial world.
production optimize-attribute location 18
production optimize-attribute block 18
production optimize-attribute task 18
production optimize-attribute object 18
production optimize-attribute on 8
production optimize-attribute below 8
production optimize-attribute clear 9
production optimize-attribute left-of 8
production optimize-attribute right-of 8


## Propose initialize-eight-men-raft when its conditions below hold.
sp {eight-men-raft*propose*initialize-eight-men-raft
   (state <s> ^superstate nil ^world <w> -^name)
-->
   (<s> ^operator <o> + >)
   (<o> ^name initialize-eight-men-raft ^task-operator false)
}

sp {eight-men-raft*apply*initialize-eight-men-raft
   (state <s> ^operator.name initialize-eight-men-raft ^world <w>)
   (<w> ^objects <objs>)
-->
